- How would you extend to multiple arenas or resizing?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of low-level synchronization primitives, memory ordering, and practical reuse of barriers without locks.

## Key Concepts
- Atomic fetch_add and compare_exchange
- Memory_order_acquire/release or relaxed with correct ordering
- Sense-reversing barrier for reuse
- Spin-wait costs and NUMA locality

## Code Example
```c
typedef struct { atomic_int count; atomic_int sense; int N; } barrier_t;

void barrier_init(barrier_t *b, int N){
  atomic_init(&b->count, 0);
  atomic_init(&b->sense, 0);
  b->N = N;
}

void barrier_wait(barrier_t *b, int *local_sense){
  int my_sense = !*local_sense;
  if (atomic_fetch_add_explicit(&b->count, 1, memory_order_acq_rel) + 1 == b->N){
    atomic_store_explicit(&b->count, 0, memory_order_relaxed);
    atomic_xor_explicit(&b->sense, 1, memory_order_release);
  } else {
    while (atomic_load_explicit(&b->sense, memory_order_acquire) != *local_sense){
      // spin
    }
  }
  *local_sense = my_sense;
}
```

